    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Client Intake Classifier\n\nFor agencies and freelancers who take project requests through a form and need those requests sorted by type before anyone reads them. An LLM classifies each submission and routes it automatically, instead of a human triaging every lead by hand.\n\n**Flow at a glance:** Form submission → AI classification → route by category → notify + log.\n\n**Setup:** Requires a Google Gemini (PaLM) API credential, a Gmail OAuth2 credential (used for all internal + client notification emails), and a Google Sheets OAuth2 credential (used for logging). Update the target spreadsheet ID and sender addresses to your own before running.\n\n**Support:** Questions or issues — ask in the [n8n Community Forum](https://community.n8n.io).",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 620
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1680,
        -1250
      ],
      "id": "sticky-10822",
      "name": "Sticky: Overview"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Classify the submission\n\nThe form's project description is sent to Gemini, which sorts it into one of five categories — simple_automation, ai_workflow, custom_integration, ambiguous, or invalid — and flags whether an \"invalid\" submission still shows partial automation intent.\n\nA structured output schema keeps the model's response in a fixed shape so the rest of the workflow can route on it reliably.",
        "height": 220,
        "width": 700
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -940,
        -1300
      ],
      "id": "sticky-15895",
      "name": "Sticky: Classification"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2. Handle the result, then route\n\nIf classification succeeds, the category is attached to the submission. If it fails (after 3 retries, 5s apart), it's marked as a distinct system_error state instead of crashing the workflow.\n\nEither way, the submission is logged to Google Sheets — this happens independently of whether the notification emails below succeed, so every submission is recorded even if a category or email step fails.\n\nA Switch node then routes the submission into one of five paths based on its category.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 560
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -360,
        -1520
      ],
      "id": "sticky-23961",
      "name": "Sticky: Routing & Logging"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3. Standard categories\n\nsimple_automation, ai_workflow, and custom_integration all follow the same two-step pattern: an internal email alerts the team to the new lead, then a confirmation email goes to the client.",
        "height": 650,
        "width": 240
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        -780
      ],
      "id": "sticky-42921",
      "name": "Sticky: Standard Notification Pattern"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 4. Ambiguous & system error — shared path\n\nBoth land here first, sharing one internal-alert email. After the notification, a check splits them apart: system errors get a \"we're looking into it\" client email; ambiguous submissions get a \"we need more detail\" client email.",
        "height": 75,
        "width": 1140
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        215
      ],
      "id": "sticky-55976",
      "name": "Sticky: Ambiguous & System Error Handling"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 5. Invalid submissions\n\nChecked for partial automation intent. If some intent is present, the team is notified and the client gets a follow-up email. If there's none, the submission is logged (above) and the flow ends here — no notification is sent.",
        "height": 180,
        "width": 240
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -60,
        280
      ],
      "id": "sticky-1583",
      "name": "Sticky: Invalid Submissions"
    }
  ],
